{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01RpHoLtxcPjd6uKMsehjY7B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem:** go-unix-utils is a specification-driven experiment that regenerates GNU coreutils/moreutils in Go, verified via differential testing against Homebrew reference binaries. The goal is to stress-test an AI code generation pipeline, not ship utilities.\n\n**Architecture:** Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Human writes PRDs/use cases, mage-claude-orchestrator generates Go code into `cmd/` and `pkg/`, and `pkg/testutils` runs differential tests comparing Go binaries against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Current state:** Release 02.0 (true, false, yes, basename, dirname) and earlier releases are implemented. Release 02.1 (tee) has specs complete and implementation committed (Task 340, commit 4a8eea3). The implementation exists but the differential test task has not been proposed yet.\n\n**Current release:** 02.1 — one use case remains: rel02.1-uc001-tee. Implementation is done; differential tests are next.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 02.1 has a single use case (tee). The implementation was completed in Task 340. Per P2, tests are split from implementation. The next task is the differential test for `cmd/tee`.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"rel02.1-uc001-tee: differential tests for cmd/tee\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - cmd/tee/main.go (existing tee implementation to test)\n      - docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel-02.1.yaml (test cases for tee)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel02.1-uc001-tee.yaml (use case success criteria)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (find the tee PRD, filename matches prd*-tee.yaml)\n      - pkg/testutils/difftest.go (DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests harness)\n      - cmd/true/true_test.go (example differential test file for pattern reference)\n      - cmd/basename/basename_test.go (example differential test file for pattern reference)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/tee/tee_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Differential tests for tee against gtee reference binary\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: |\n          Write differential tests exercising tee core behavior: read stdin,\n          write to stdout, and write to one or more output files simultaneously.\n          Verify exit code, stdout, and file contents match the reference binary.\n      - id: R2\n        text: |\n          Write differential tests for the -a (append) flag: verify that tee\n          appends to existing files rather than truncating them, matching\n          reference binary behavior.\n      - id: R3\n        text: |\n          Write differential tests for error conditions: writing to a\n          nonexistent directory, writing to a read-only file, and passing\n          --version/--help flags. Verify exit codes and stderr match the\n          reference binary.\n      - id: R4\n        text: |\n          Write differential tests for multiple output files: verify tee writes\n          identical content to all specified files and stdout simultaneously,\n          matching reference binary behavior.\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: |\n          Use the standard differential testing pattern from the project:\n          testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\") for the Go binary, exec.LookPath(\"gtee\")\n          for the Homebrew GNU coreutils reference binary, and\n          testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests) to compare outputs.\n      - id: D2\n        text: |\n          Call t.Skip if the reference binary gtee is not found in PATH, per the\n          project's graceful-skip protocol. Do not attempt to install the binary.\n      - id: D3\n        text: |\n          For tests that verify file output, use t.TempDir() to create temporary\n          directories and set DiffTest.WorkDir accordingly. After RunDiffTests\n          completes, compare file contents written by both binaries.\n      - id: D4\n        text: |\n          Set LC_ALL=C in the test environment per project convention to ensure\n          consistent error message formatting between Go and reference binaries.\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: cmd/tee/tee_test.go exists and contains a TestDiff function\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/tee/ passes when gtee is available in PATH\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/tee/ skips gracefully when gtee is not in PATH\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: Tests cover basic piping, append mode, multiple files, and error cases\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"go vet ./cmd/tee/ reports no issues\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27558,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27558},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d74bc26f-6328-420a-a876-625e77ef74c9","uuid":"60ee9453-13e2-4a2a-b1e6-ca77fa849609"}
